															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/enderdragon101" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6602770); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6602770&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610075812" alt="EnderDragon101" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6602770)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/enderdragon101" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6602770); return false;" >EnderDragon101</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608241910 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2020 21:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847231">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> never thought the GOC is heartless enough to shoot down an innocent alien cargo ship, but man were we wrong.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-XXXX is an alien cargo ship that was shot down by the GOC and crashed 20 miles west of San Francisco, pieces of the SCP-XXXX was too badly damaged to know the original shape or size of it, but a name was discovered “Galactic.Co”</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 is the Survivors of the incident and appears to be a combination of a human and a orca, they are strong, intelligent and can swim very fast, but because of the GOC they are stuck here with no way for them to contact their home world, but they are cooperative.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 are monoliths that contains SCP-XXXX-3 which is gravitonium, SCP-XXXX-2 is made of an unknown element never seen before but are considered safe, SCP-XXXX-3 on the other hand is highly dangerous and is considered unpredictable, SCP-XXXX-3 has the ability to manipulate gravity which can result in casualties, but it is also useful because of its ability to make artificial gravity and SCP-XXXX-2 is the only thing capable of containing it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> there’s 3 Hooks with this SCP idea.</p>
<p>The first being SCP-XXXX-3 the gravitonium, if the Foundation managed to create an SCP-XXXX-2 then they would be able to use SCP-XXXX-3 for artificial gravity, this SCP could change the Foundation in the near future if successfully contained and controlled.</p>
<p>The second is because some of SCP-XXXX-2 with SCP-XXXX-3 was sucked out and landing in places where there’s more of SCP-XXXX-3 underground and worse where GoI are digging them up, fortunately only the foundation has the SCP-XXXX-2’s.</p>
<p>And the third is the idea of whether or not the SCP-XXXX/1’s are ever going to see home again or if the GOC finds out about them, how would they react.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> this SCP idea is split up in 2 forms, 1 being about the SCP itself and 1 about Project Space Cannon and why the GOC built it, there is also going to be a series of events that took place in the ship before its doom, the trouble of keeping this from the public and a series of test involving SCP-XXXX-2 and 3.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
